  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959190/assets/13b9598c77cd522d0d3aeee4f5abd2390822431aa49ed787b73a110113ab821c.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=25,$ shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+{0}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =25 \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{25} \\\\ x+4 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ x & =-4\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-9,0)$ and $(1,0).$",
